# AI Agent Contribution Policy

Inspired by the Hugging Face Transformers agentic contribution policy.

## Coordination before coding

Before proposing any PR or diff:

1. Check whether a GitHub Issue already covers this work
2. Check for overlapping open PRs:
   ```bash
   gh pr list --repo <org>/cosmo-soft --state open --search "<keywords>"
   ```
3. If an open PR already addresses the same change — **stop** and explain the overlap
4. Do not work on someone else's issue without explicit maintainer approval in the issue thread

## Fail-closed behaviour

If any of the following are true, **do not output a PR-ready diff** — instead return a short explanation of what is missing:

- No coordination evidence (no Issue link, no approval comment)
- The proposed change duplicates an existing open PR
- The change is trivial busywork (single typo, isolated whitespace, one-line lint fix)

## PR description requirements for AI-assisted work

Every PR where AI assistance was used must include:

- Link to the Issue and any coordination/approval comment
- Statement confirming the change does not duplicate an existing PR
- Test commands run and their output
- `Assisted-by: <tool-name>` commit trailer

## Atomic changes

Make the smallest reversible change that addresses the task.
Do not refactor unrelated code in the same PR.
